lly  dangerous pirate as we are about to see  so just keep all that in mind bounties  are hype but they are ultimately just a  weapon that the world government has at  their disposal and in the end they use  it in any way that will best serve their  own ends so at number 10 we start off  strong with luffy's old bounty of 1.5  billion berries this was actually  luffy's sixth bounty and happened after  he was recognized as sabo's further  tying him to the revolutionaries the  most dangerous organization to the world  government and after the events of whole  cake island and his defeat of yonko  commander charlotte cracker whose bounty  was 860 million and big mom's strongest  commander charlotte kanakuri whose  bounty was 1.057 billion with this  bounty luffy also gained the title the  fifth emperor thanks to the legend the  big news morgans as the title suggests  this bounty catapulted luffy above all  yonko commanders and only the yonko were  left for him to pass to be fair luffy  was catapulted ahead of all yonko  commanders with known bounties  specifically but we still don't know  some bounties like ben beckman's which  could potentially be quite high number  nine is none other than yonko blackbeard  at  2.2476 billion berries this is probably  one of the most hyped top 10 lists ever  when number 10 and 9 are luffy and yonko  blackbeard but it's true unless  blackbeard's bounty has changed off  screen which is definitely possible as  we'll discuss later his current bounty  is less than luffy's blackbeard was  previously a member of the whitebeard  pirate then he became a warlord he  defeated ace one of whitebeard's  strongest commanders in battle he went  on to recruit multiple level 6 prisoners  at impel down as sengoku described it he  took the strongest of the world's most  dangerous prisoners sengoku says even  one level 6 prisoner can cause  unimaginable chaos simply by  infiltrating a nation so you can imagine  that multiple working together under the  master planner blackbeard is much more  concerning of course he also  participated in the summit war at  marineford and you can even say he was  the biggest winner in it not only did he  get strong crew members he also killed  yonko whitebeard the strongest man in  the world who to be fair was very  injured and blackbeard sort of just  swooped in after the heavy lifting was  done but still it's a very legend  building detail that people can say  about blackbeard he then stole the  guragura no a fruit that is said to be  able to destroy the world and is  considered to be the strongest paramecia  fruit and became the first character we  know of to wield two devil fruits even  though that's supposed to be impossible  finally he to use robin's own word  obliterated marco and the remnants of  the whitebeard pirates during the  payback war and in doing so solidified  his position as the newest yonko thus  it's no surprise he received such a high  bounty next for number eight number  seven and number six we have a three-way  tie surprisingly and now we really start  to break from tradition in regards to  how bounty levels are determined just  recently it's been revealed that monkey  d luffy eustis kid and trafalgar d water  law all received a three billion barry  bounty i don't want to take anything  away from kid and law they killed it  this arc they've been amazing together  they beat a yonko namely big mom who had  a bounty of over 4 billion so i'm  totally cool with their combined bounty  being higher than big mom's bounty but  the problem is luffy got the same bounty  even though he took down kaido alone for  all intents and purposes despite some  other characters hurting kaido a bit  before their match plus there's the fact  that luffy just awakened the most  ridiculous power in the world that the  world government arguably fears the most  these bounties only make sense if a they  don't consider the details of the  battles just the fact that these three  supernova be too yonko or b if the world  government wants to avoid putting any  extra spotlight on luffy then absolutely  necessary the latter is probably the  case as we saw them freak out over  luffy's gear 5 aka awakened sun god nika  form being featured on his wanted poster  along with the d initial in his name  they want to spin the story like these  three roughly equal supernova beat these  two yonko and that's that this way they  hope to limit the attention on luffy the  joy boy and warrior of liberation of the  new era who if legend is correct is the  biggest threat to the world government  because he is destined to free all those  under the government's control thus in  my view luffy after beating the  strongest creature in the world and  awakening the most ridiculous power that  hasn't been seen in 800 years deserves  the highest bounty we've seen to date  but because it would actually be bad for  the government to put the spotlight on  the worry of liberation they purposely  used the wanted poster to hide the truth  as much as they could showing that in  the end the wanted posters are but tools  for the government to use for their own  benefit and not objective or scientific  measurements of threat level or strength  number five is yonko shanks at  4.0489 billion berries and believe it or  not now our red-haired boy has the  highest known active bounty in the  series this serves the government well  because they know shanks is not the one  to cause unnecessary trouble and the  five elders are even willing to secretly  meet with him without trying to capture  him showing that they are not too  worried about him obviously in their  view luffy is a bigger threat but they  still gave luffy a lower bounty for  tactical reasons number four and number  three are big mom at 4.388 billion and  kaido at  4.6111 billion both of their bounties  have become inactive in light of their  recent defeats by the three supernova  kid law and luffy it's funny to look at  how the world government uses bounties  to help manipulate public perception in  light of recent events the public might  assume the two most dangerous living  yonko with the highest known bounties  have been defeated and now the  government's job must be easier because  instead of taking down the strongest  creature in the world and his legendary  yonko partner they only gotta take down  three upstarts who are weaker  individually than either of the yonko in  reality the situation is much worse  though as we know since in kaido's case  he was more or less close with the world  government close enough to allow cp-0  agents to chill in his territory however  luffy who physically beat the strongest  creature in the world cannot be  controlled and will continue to seek  liberation for others which will require  eventually the downfall of the world  government and he won't compromise his  ideals so even though we know kaido was  less of a threat to the world government  they don't let luffy pass kaido's bounty  or even big mom's bounty number two is  whitebeard at 5.046 billion this one is  obviously also inactive since whitebeard  is dead after all however when he lived  he not only possessed the power to  destroy the world via the guragura no me  he was also viewed as the strongest man  in the world and the man closest to one  piece he fought on equal terms with his  rival pirate king gold d roger and as a  younger man he arguably could have  become the next pirate king and found  the one piece but he wasn't interested  because he prioritized his crew aka his  family he was uninterested in the one  piece and in taking down the world  government until they wanted to execute  his family and so it was safe for the  world government to let him keep the  highest active bounty while he lived  furthermore when he died a marine ford  that again helped the government's  public image in the sense that they  could look back and say they helped take  down the biggest threat in the world and  thus the world is now a safer place and  even the strongest man in the world  wasn't strong enough to beat the world  government lastly number one is the  great pirate gold d roger the former  pirate king as with luffy the government  wanted to erase the d from his name and  in his case succeeded by changing his  name to gold roger on the wanted poster  this is a little clue to us that luffy  has reached a similar status in the eyes  of the world government and i of course  think he's more dangerous as i've  explained because roger didn't have the  sun god nika fruit furthermore as roger  mentioned before he knew he was too  early so he wasn't planning to take down  the world government in fact we were  told he helped the world government and  celestial dragons at god valley when he  worked together with the hero of the  marines garp to take down the rock's  pirates then he handed himself over to  the world government when he was sick  and so the world government looked  strong because they got to publicly  execute him the man with the highest  bounty ever as far as we know from the  government's perspective they might  purposely never want to give any other  enemy a higher bounty because as things  stand they can always publicly maintain  the image that if they could beat and  execute the pirate king goldie roger  then no one should think that a pirate  with a lower bounty can take them down  in this way the government maintains the  appearance of strength even though  behind the scenes the situation is way  different and way worse for them and so  these last bounty reveals have  completely changed the game and the way  we view bounties now dragon might in  fact have a lower bounty than he  deserves even if he's the world's worst  criminal because the government doesn't  want to give him too much attention or  hype that being said i should clarify  that i've discussed known bounties in  this video and it's quite likely that  future revealed bounties will change the  make